0..65 Comment "// A motive that names a path type, a bridge type or a flow type."
66..68 Comment "//"
69..146 Comment "// A motive maps each index to a type. An eliminator reads its motive at each"
147..196 Comment "// index, so the motive must be a function value."
197..199 Comment "//"
200..278 Comment "// The body of a function is a computation, and a type is a value. So the body"
279..356 Comment "// writes `return` before the type, as it does before any value. The function"
357..412 Comment "// is a value too, so the definition returns its thunk."
413..415 Comment "//"
416..431 Comment "// - see: #6491"
